- @next: Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher and her Conservative Party have won a landslide victory to a second term in office. 

@next

Her rival Labour Party bled votes and seats to a new alliance between the social democrats and liberals.

Overall this means a continuation of the Thatcher cabinet's policy of cooperation with Sri Lanka, the nature of this victory could embolden Thatcher to pursue even her goals both domestic and foreign with less restraint.
